  "result": "Shell completion now treats `#` as a normal character, so `cli a#b` is split into `[\"cli\", \"a#b\"]` instead of losing everything from the `#` onward. The parser and shell-completion tests pass (68 passed). I didn't run the full test suite.\n\n- **Fix:** in `split_arg_string` (`src/click/shell_completion.py`), I turned off the tokenizer's comment handling with `lex.commenters = \"\"`.\n- **Tests:** I added three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli a#b`, `cli #a`, and `cli 'my #file` (with an unclosed quote).\n- **Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` has a new unreleased 8.5.1 section with an entry for this fix.\n\nI skipped the optional end-to-end completion test from the plan, since the parser tests already cover the cause.",
